[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: web_server_0
diagnosis_text:
- Affected component: The HTTP application layer on web_server_0 (apache2 service) is down; there is no web server bound to TCP/80.
- Mechanism: Clients resolve web0.local to 10.200.0.3 (confirmed on host_1_1_1_1 via getent). The IP path is healthy (ICMP from host_1_1_1_1 to 10.200.0.3 has 0% loss). However, because no process is listening on port 80 on web_server_0, TCP SYNs receive an immediate RST/connection failure. This presents to users as a page that “never loads” or fails quickly, despite routing being up.
- Localization: On web_server_0, netstat/ss show no listener on 0.0.0.0:80—only 127.0.0.11 (DNS stub) is listening. systemctl reports apache2 is “Active: inactive (dead)”. As a control, web_server_1 is correctly listening on 0.0.0.0:80 with apache2 processes present.
- Root cause: The apache2 service on web_server_0 is stopped, leaving no HTTP listener on port 80.
- Corrective fix: Restart the HTTP service on the server, not the network core. On web_server_0, run: systemctl restart apache2 && systemctl enable apache2. Verify with ss -lntp (should show 0.0.0.0:80, users:(“apache2”)) and a curl from host_1_1_1_1 to http://web0.local should return an HTTP response. No OSPF or core routing changes are required; the network path is functioning.

=== END ===